WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.537 --> 00:00:15.159
I was horrified by what Nemo had done.

2
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.821
No matter what he had suffered at the hands of those men, he had no right to kill

3
00:00:19.861 --> 00:00:20.921
them by sinking their ship.

4
00:00:21.881 --> 00:00:26.763
And he had made me a witness to his terrible vengeance, perhaps even an accomplice!

5
00:00:27.823 --> 00:00:31.284
I spent a few hours with Ned and Conseil, who had remained in my cabin.

6
00:00:32.192 --> 00:00:36.074
We did not have much to say, being too stunned by the events of that day.

7
00:00:37.134 --> 00:00:39.235
Later I went to the deserted gallery.

8
00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:44.717
I consulted the instruments, and found that the Nautilus was swiftly heading toward the northern seas.

9
00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.899
That night we crossed two hundred leagues of the Atlantic.

10
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:55.582
I returned to my cabin, but could not sleep because that horrible scene of destruction kept replaying before

11
00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.062
my eyes.

12
00:00:57.043 --> 00:01:02.125
From that day forward, I lost all track of time because the clocks were stopped onboard.

13
00:01:03.526 --> 00:01:07.249
For the next few weeks, The Nautilus was underwater almost constantly.

14
00:01:08.149 --> 00:01:11.692
There were no new marks on the map, so I had no idea where we were.

15
00:01:12.773 --> 00:01:13.853
I saw nothing of Nemo.

16
00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.176
As a matter of fact, I didn't see a single crew member.

17
00:01:18.336 --> 00:01:21.398
One morning I awoke suddenly to find Ned standing over me.

18
00:01:21.418 --> 00:01:25.541
"We're going to flee tonight, Professor," he whispered.

19
00:01:25.561 --> 00:01:28.423
"There doesn't seem to be anyone in charge anymore.

20
00:01:28.743 --> 00:01:29.244
You'll be ready?"

21
00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:30.740
I sat up.

22
00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.321
"Yes, of course, but where are we?"

23
00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:38.202
"The fog just lifted for a moment and I sighted land about twenty miles away.

24
00:01:38.602 --> 00:01:39.723
I don't know what country it is."

25
00:01:40.763 --> 00:01:41.323
"How's the weather?"

26
00:01:41.343 --> 00:01:45.304
"The sea is bad and the wind is violent," replied Ned.

27
00:01:45.324 --> 00:01:48.725
"But twenty miles in the small boat doesn't frighten me."

28
00:01:48.745 --> 00:01:52.846
"I'll follow you, Ned, even if the sea swallows us up."

29
00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:54.887
"There," I thought.

30
00:01:55.507 --> 00:01:58.668
I had made up my mind and finally agreed to his escape plan.

31
00:01:59.784 --> 00:02:01.485
I dressed quickly and went up to the platform.

32
00:02:02.486 --> 00:02:06.928
The sea was so rough that I could barely keep my balance, but I knew that land was

33
00:02:07.008 --> 00:02:08.269
somewhere out there in the fog.

34
00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:13.431
I returned to the empty gallery, both wishing and not wishing to see Nemo.

35
00:02:14.132 --> 00:02:15.092
What could I have said to him?

36
00:02:16.113 --> 00:02:17.934
Could I have hid my horror at what he had done?

37
00:02:18.694 --> 00:02:20.535
No, it was better that we did not meet.

38
00:02:21.676 --> 00:02:26.699
I stayed by myself all day and avoided Ned and Conseil for fear of betraying our secret.

39
00:02:27.699 --> 00:02:30.477
I dined at six that night, even though I wasn't hungry.

40
00:02:31.498 --> 00:02:34.380
I forced myself to eat so that I might keep up my strength.

41
00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.482
At half past six, Ned came to my cabin.

42
00:02:37.502 --> 00:02:42.205
"We won't see each other again before our departure at ten o'clock," he said.

43
00:02:42.225 --> 00:02:46.748
"The moon will not have risen yet, so we'll take advantage of the darkness to escape.

44
00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:50.991
Come to the small boat; Conseil and I will be waiting for you there."

45
00:02:52.012 --> 00:02:53.853
Ned left without giving me time to respond.

46
00:02:54.614 --> 00:02:57.396
Wishing to check the course of the Nautilus, I went to the gallery.

47
00:02:58.432 --> 00:03:00.513
We were heading northeast at a rapid speed.

48
00:03:01.573 --> 00:03:07.036
I spent the next hour slowly walking around the room and admiring all the natural and man-made treasures

49
00:03:07.076 --> 00:03:08.456
that Captain Nemo had collected.

50
00:03:09.537 --> 00:03:14.118
Returning to my room, I dressed warmly and gathered my notes on underwater life.

51
00:03:15.139 --> 00:03:18.120
I stretched out on my bed in an attempt to quiet my nerves.

52
00:03:19.181 --> 00:03:25.083
In my mind I reviewed our months of captivity: our arrival onboard the submarine, the attack of the

53
00:03:25.143 --> 00:03:30.930
natives, the visit to the coral cemetery, the underwater passage to the Mediterranean, the discovery of the South

54
00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:33.031
Pole, and everything else that had happened.

55
00:03:34.452 --> 00:03:37.673
All these scenes passed before my eyes as if I were viewing a play.

56
00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:43.617
Captain Nemo seemed to grow enormously, and his features assumed superhuman proportions.

57
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:48.939
He was no longer my equal but a man of the waters, the genie of the sea.

58
00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.081
It was now 9:30.

59
00:03:51.761 --> 00:03:54.462
I held my head between my hands to keep it from bursting.

60
00:03:55.463 --> 00:03:57.244
There was another long half hour to wait.

61
00:03:58.064 --> 00:04:00.846
After a while I heard the distant sound of organ music.

62
00:04:01.786 --> 00:04:05.789
Captain Nemo was in the gallery, and I had to pass through that room to escape!

63
00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:07.950
But it was now nearly ten o'clock.

64
00:04:08.991 --> 00:04:12.393
The moment had come for me to leave my cabin and join my companions.

65
00:04:13.414 --> 00:04:16.416
I crept along the passage until I reached the door of the gallery.

66
00:04:17.096 --> 00:04:18.297
I opened the door gently.

67
00:04:19.277 --> 00:04:23.100
The room was completely dark, but the captain was still playing the organ.

68
00:04:24.156 --> 00:04:29.740
I moved so slowly across the room that it took me five full minutes to reach the door

69
00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:30.481
to the library.

70
00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:35.604
I was about to open it when a sigh from Captain Nemo nailed me to the spot.

71
00:04:36.325 --> 00:04:37.525
I knew that he was standing up.

72
00:04:38.586 --> 00:04:42.729
He came toward me silently, gliding like a ghost rather than walking.

73
00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:46.952
He was sobbing, and I heard him say, "Enough!

74
00:04:47.832 --> 00:04:52.756
Enough!" Was that a confession or at least some expression of remorse?

75
00:04:53.408 --> 00:04:54.889
Could he see me there in the darkness?

76
00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:56.090
I didn't know.

77
00:04:57.111 --> 00:05:00.793
In desperation I rushed through the library and up the stairs to the platform.

78
00:05:01.774 --> 00:05:04.836
I climbed into the small boat, where I found Ned and Conseil waiting for me.

79
00:05:04.856 --> 00:05:06.257
"Let's go!"

80
00:05:06.777 --> 00:05:07.337
I exclaimed.

81
00:05:08.298 --> 00:05:11.180
Ned began to loosen the bolts that held the boat to the submarine.

82
00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.482
Suddenly we heard loud voices from below.

83
00:05:15.162 --> 00:05:16.423
Had someone discovered our flight?

84
00:05:16.443 --> 00:05:19.445
"Whirlpool! Whirlpool!"

85
00:05:19.926 --> 00:05:20.666
voices cried.

86
00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.208
"They're shouting about a giant whirlpool!"

87
00:05:23.644 --> 00:05:24.325
said Conseil.

88
00:05:24.345 --> 00:05:25.906
"They're not after us."

89
00:05:27.227 --> 00:05:27.947
My heart sunk.

90
00:05:28.608 --> 00:05:33.231
Apparently we were now in those Norwegian waters famous for a dangerous whirlpool.

91
00:05:33.931 --> 00:05:35.492
No vessel had ever survived it.

92
00:05:36.393 --> 00:05:41.997
We would never know if this had happened accidentally or if Captain Nemo had deliberately sent the Nautilus

93
00:05:42.077 --> 00:05:46.300
straight into the whirlpool in order to destroy the submarine and everyone aboard!

94
00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:52.584
Dreadful sounds filled our ears as the submarine spiraled toward the center of the whirlpool.

95
00:05:53.636 --> 00:05:56.818
Dizzy, and overcome with fear, I grabbed Conseil's hand.

96
00:05:56.838 --> 00:05:58.339
"Hold on!"

97
00:05:58.780 --> 00:05:59.300
shouted Ned.

98
00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:05.084
"We may be saved if we cling to the Nautilus and—" Just then we heard a crashing sound

99
00:06:05.404 --> 00:06:07.626
and the small boat was torn from the submarine.

100
00:06:08.647 --> 00:06:11.328
My head struck something metal, and I lost consciousness.

101
00:06:12.389 --> 00:06:14.591
I woke up in a Norwegian fisherman's cottage.

102
00:06:15.311 --> 00:06:17.132
How I got here, I have no idea.

103
00:06:18.513 --> 00:06:23.681
To my great relief, my two companions were safe and sound too, and at my bedside holding my

104
00:06:23.722 --> 00:06:28.326
hands. I must now wait for a month for the next steamship to France.

105
00:06:29.307 --> 00:06:32.970
So it is here where I'm reviewing my amazing adventures with Captain Nemo.

106
00:06:33.971 --> 00:06:38.975
I traveled 20,000 leagues under the sea with him, but I have no idea what happened to him

107
00:06:39.556 --> 00:06:40.697
or his beloved Nautilus.

108
00:06:41.698 --> 00:06:46.102
I still have so many questions: Will the waves ever carry his manuscript to land?

109
00:06:47.003 --> 00:06:48.204
Will I learn his real name?

110
00:06:48.972 --> 00:06:52.094
Will the nationality of the sunken ship reveal his home country?

111
00:06:53.155 --> 00:06:58.458
Will I ever know what happened to his family and why he needed to seek revenge so desperately?

112
00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:00.699
I hope these answers come.

113
00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:06.803
But I also hope that Captain Nemo's powerful vessel conquered the whirlpool and that he still inhabits the

114
00:07:06.863 --> 00:07:14.767
sea. Perhaps contemplating the wonders of the sea will restore his soul—and forever extinguish the spirit of vengeance

115
00:07:14.807 --> 00:07:15.868
that burns within him.
